  "notes": "よす is a casual/colloquial verb meaning to stop or quit an action. Common in informal speech.\n\nTRANSITIVITY:\n- Type: ⟦{他動詞|たどうし}→他動詞：10418_tadoushi⟧ (transitive)\n- Takes ⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧ particle: ⟦タバコ→たばこ：02909_tabako⟧⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧よす (quit smoking)\n\nREGISTER:\nCasual to rough. Often used in commands or strong suggestions. Not appropriate in formal settings.\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n- よせ! / よせ⟦よ→よ：09475_yo⟧!: Stop it! (imperative, rough)\n- よし⟦なさい→なさる：01307_nasaru⟧: Stop that (softer command, often to children)\n- ～⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧よした⟦{方|ほう}→方：01139_hou⟧⟦が→が：00051_ga⟧⟦いい→いい：00118_ii⟧: You'd better quit ~\n- よそう: Let's stop / I'll stop (volitional)\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- ⟦やめる→やめる：00909_yameru⟧: to stop, quit (more neutral, widely usable)\n- ⟦{止|と}める→止める：00678_tomeru⟧: to stop (more formal, also physical stopping)",
